G44-48 — HIGH — Repo-Local Git Config Audit Precedence & --no-includes / --show-scope / Case-Sensitivity Gaps in G44-38
Affected Component: G44-38 / G44-45 Git configuration auditor.
Preconditions: Hostile .git/config containing include.path, includeIf.*, extensions.worktreeConfig=true + .git/config.worktree, duplicate singleton keys, empty values, or URL-scoped http.<url>.extraHeader.
Failure Scenario: Calling git config --local --list --null without --no-includes causes Git to parse included external files during the audit itself; omitting --show-scope --show-origin fails to verify that no system/global/worktree/command config leaked in; CLI -c http.extraHeader= does not override URL-scoped http.<url>.extraHeader keys.
Security Impact: Undetected config injection, unauthorized HTTP header/proxy/credential-helper activation, or operational failure on canonical URL redirects (http.followRedirects=false).
Why Existing Design Fails: Specified git config --local --list --null without --no-includes, --show-scope, --show-origin, duplicate-singleton rejection, empty-value rejection, or .git/config.worktree absence check.
